    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "step-1",
        "kind": "active",
        "text": "Heat the oven to 375\u00b0F (190\u00b0C). Line a 12-cup muffin tin with paper liners."
      },
      {
        "id": "step-2",
        "kind": "active",
        "text": "In a large bowl, whisk together the 1 and 3/4 cups of flour, the baking powder, baking soda and salt."
      },
      {
        "id": "step-3",
        "kind": "active",
        "text": "In a second bowl, rub the lemon zest into the granulated sugar with your fingertips until it is fragrant and looks like damp sand."
      },
      {
        "id": "step-4",
        "kind": "active",
        "text": "Whisk the melted butter into the lemon sugar, then the eggs one at a time, then the yogurt, milk, lemon juice and vanilla until smooth."
      },
      {
        "id": "step-5",
        "kind": "active",
        "text": "Toss the blueberries with the 1 tablespoon of flour so they don't sink."
      },
      {
        "id": "step-6",
        "kind": "active",
        "text": "Pour the wet ingredients into the dry ones and fold with a spatula until only a few streaks of flour remain. Gently fold in the blueberries. The batter will be thick."
      },
      {
        "id": "step-7",
        "kind": "active",
        "text": "Divide the batter among the muffin cups; they will be quite full. Sprinkle the tops with the turbinado sugar."
      },
      {
        "id": "step-8",
        "kind": "active",
        "text": "Bake for 20 to 22 minutes, until the tops are golden and a toothpick in the center of a muffin comes out clean."
      },
      {
        "id": "step-9",
        "kind": "active",
        "text": "Cool the muffins in the tin for 5 minutes, then move them to a rack."
      }
    ],
